From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: msm8916-openwrt-clean <dev@localhost>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plugin-manager: halve the port-probe settle timers

ModemManager will not complete a device support check until two fixed
timers have expired, even when every port has already been probed:

  MIN_WAIT_TIME_MSECS      2000  -- delay before the first port is probed
  MIN_PROBING_TIME_MSECS   4000  -- floor on the whole probing phase
  EXTRA_PROBING_TIME_MSECS 2000 WITH_UDEV / 4000 without

device_context_complete() returns early while either of the last two is
still pending, so on a platform that reports ports through hotplug
scripts -- OpenWrt builds ModemManager with -Dudev=false -- the support
check takes at least 4 s even when the QMI probe itself is sub-second.

Measured on a Qualcomm MSM8916 modem whose 9 wwan ports are all
re-enumerated in one burst after a remoteproc restart: the QMI probe
starts at +2000 ms and the modem object is created at +4000 ms, in 9 of
11 consecutive restarts, while the probe step itself (start/QMI/done)
completes inside one second. That is 4 s of every post-restart recovery
spent waiting on a timer, not on the modem.

Halve all three, preserving the existing relationships (MIN_PROBING stays
above MIN_WAIT, and the non-udev extra wait stays twice the udev one).

The late-port safety net is unchanged in kind: device_context_port_added()
still restarts the extra probing timer for every port that arrives after
the check began, and device_context_complete() still refuses to finish
while that timer is pending.

Signed-off-by: msm8916-openwrt-clean <dev@localhost>
---
 src/mm-plugin-manager.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mm-plugin-manager.c b/src/mm-plugin-manager.c
index f8cf009..f5983f2 100644
--- a/src/mm-plugin-manager.c
+++ b/src/mm-plugin-manager.c
@@ -715,20 +715,20 @@ port_context_new (MMPluginManager *self,
 /* Device context */
 
 /* Time to wait for ports to appear before starting to probe the first one */
-#define MIN_WAIT_TIME_MSECS 2000
+#define MIN_WAIT_TIME_MSECS 1000
 
 /* Time to wait for other ports to appear once the first port is exposed
  * (needs to be > MIN_WAIT_TIME_MSECS!!) */
-#define MIN_PROBING_TIME_MSECS 4000
+#define MIN_PROBING_TIME_MSECS 2000
 
 /* Additional time to wait for other ports to appear after the last port is
  * exposed in the system. Longer time when not using udev, as we rely on
  * mmcli --report-kernel-event events to report new port additions, e.g.
  * via openwrt hotplug scripts. */
 #if defined WITH_UDEV
-# define EXTRA_PROBING_TIME_MSECS 2000
+# define EXTRA_PROBING_TIME_MSECS 1000
 #else
-# define EXTRA_PROBING_TIME_MSECS 4000
+# define EXTRA_PROBING_TIME_MSECS 2000
 #endif
 
 /* The wait time we define must always be less than the probing time */
